.TH "knockr" "1" "2026-08-06"
.P
.SH NAME
.P
knockr - port knocking utility for tcp/udp
.P
.SH SYNOPSIS
.P
\fBknockr\fR [options.\&.\&.\&] hostname-or-ip-address port1,port2.\&.\&.\&
.br
\fBknockr\fR [options.\&.\&.\&] profile-name
.P
.SH DESCRIPTION
.P
\fBknockr\fR, in the order of port(s) specified, opens a connection (tcp) or sends a
packet (udp) to one or more ports at a hostname or IP address.\& Hostnames are
resolved once and a single address is pinned for the entire sequence.\&
.P
.SH OPTIONS
.P
\fB-c\fR <file>
.RS 4
Profile file (default ~/.\&ssh/knockr.\&conf).\&
.P
.RE
\fB-d\fR <duration>
.RS 4
Delay between knocks (default 100ms).\&
.P
.RE
\fB-n\fR <protocol>
.RS 4
Network protocol (tcp, tcp4, tcp6, udp, udp4, udp6).\&
.P
.RE
\fB-s\fR
.RS 4
Silence all but error output.\&
.P
.RE
\fB-t\fR <duration>
.RS 4
Timeout for each knock (default 1s).\&
.P
.RE
\fB-verify\fR <ports>
.RS 4
Comma-separated tcp ports to test after knocking; exits non-zero unless
all open.\&
.P
.RE
\fB-version\fR
.RS 4
Print version and exit.\&
.P
.RE
.SH PROFILES
.P
Named knock sequences may be stored in an ssh_config-style file, by default
\fB~/.\&ssh/knockr.\&conf\fR, and invoked as \fBknockr profile-name\fR.\& The file must not
be readable by group or others (chmod 600).\& \fBhost\fR and \fBports\fR are required;
\fBprotocol\fR, \fBdelay\fR, \fBtimeout\fR, \fBsilent\fR, and \fBverify\fR are optional.\&
Command-line flags override profile values.\&
.P
.nf
.RS 4
profile router
    host 203\&.0\&.113\&.1
    ports 1234,8923,1233
    protocol udp
    verify 22
.fi
.RE
.P
.SH EXAMPLES
.P
Knock using default options:
.RS 4
knockr somehost.\&example.\&com 1234,8923,1233
.P
.RE
Using udp protocol and 50ms delay between knocks:
.RS 4
knockr -n udp -d 50ms 23.\&192.\&228.\&80 51213,8327,183,420
.P
.RE
Knock the router profile, then confirm its verify port opened:
.RS 4
knockr router
.P
.RE
